{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall make.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] translated מעיל as a mantle like the garment called a cassock, only its neck-opening was within the mantle. And our ancestors of blessed memory said that a pomegranate surrounded the mantle, and a bell between two pomegranates, for others said that the bells were not visible, only they were inside the pomegranates, and there they would sound their voice."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:50.924870939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}